thub.com/users/arnaucmd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arnaucmd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arnaucmd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arnaucmd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arnaucmd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arnaucmd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arnaucmd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arnaucmd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arnaucmd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-13T19:18:22Z","updated_at":"2026-08-13T19:18:22Z","body":"> I guess what should happen is that it should clear the oldest errors automatically (after 100,000 I guess?) so that it doesn't fill the entire memory just with errors (_and_ the nodes to represent those errors, don't forget), just like how terminals do. It's unlikely that after 100,000 errors, the oldest ones will still be relevant (it's mostly going to be the same errors printed over and over again).\n\nFor me it lags way before 100k, even if you hide or delete them, it's just text, so isn't there a deeper problem on how it's displayed? I can open a 10milion line document in notepad and it doesn't lag or crash the program.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5285317398/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5285335797","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122340#issuecomment-5285335797","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122340","id":5285335797,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABOwfS9Q","user":{"login":"arnaucmd","id":